From 24f1b47381f8d738a78256daae793fbdd87c3fdf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Showta Ishizaki <zakinko@snowrabbit.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:02:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/23] NFSD: Use rqstp->rq_bvec in nfsd_iter_write()

JIRA: https://issues.redhat.com/browse/RHEL-XXXXX

commit 1969823caf163593c82df9f9589074720bed2eea
Author: Chuck Lever <chuck.lever@oracle.com>
Date:   Tue, 6 May 2025 16:42:25 -0400

    If we can get rid of all uses of rq_vec, then it can be removed.
    Replace one use of rqstp::rq_vec with rqstp::rq_bvec.

    The feeling of layering violation grows stronger now that
    <linux/sunrpc/xdr.h> is included in fs/nfsd/vfs.c.

    Suggested-by: Christoph Hellwig <hch@infradead.org>
    Signed-off-by: Chuck Lever <chuck.lever@oracle.com>

Conflicts: RHEL 9 svc_rqst has no rq_maxpages; the bvec array is the
    fixed rq_bvec[RPCSVC_MAXPAGES], so ARRAY_SIZE(rqstp->rq_bvec) is
    passed.  The iterator direction is spelled WRITE in RHEL 9.  The
    WARN_ON_ONCE carried over from nfsd4_write() goes with the
    svc_fill_write_vector() call; xdr_buf_to_bvec() checks the bound.

Signed-off-by: Showta Ishizaki <zakinko@snowrabbit.org>
---
 fs/nfsd/vfs.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fs/nfsd/vfs.c b/fs/nfsd/vfs.c
index 9d74f70..c185e6b 100644
--- a/fs/nfsd/vfs.c
+++ b/fs/nfsd/vfs.c
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
 #include <linux/exportfs.h>
 #include <linux/writeback.h>
 #include <linux/security.h>
+#include <linux/sunrpc/xdr.h>
 
 #include "xdr3.h"
 
@@ -1221,9 +1222,9 @@ nfsd_vfs_write(struct svc_rqst *rqstp, struct svc_fh *fhp,
 	if (stable && !use_wgather)
 		flags |= RWF_SYNC;
 
-	nvecs = svc_fill_write_vector(rqstp, payload);
-	WARN_ON_ONCE(nvecs > ARRAY_SIZE(rqstp->rq_vec));
-	iov_iter_kvec(&iter, WRITE, rqstp->rq_vec, nvecs, *cnt);
+	nvecs = xdr_buf_to_bvec(rqstp->rq_bvec, ARRAY_SIZE(rqstp->rq_bvec),
+				payload);
+	iov_iter_bvec(&iter, WRITE, rqstp->rq_bvec, nvecs, *cnt);
 	since = READ_ONCE(file->f_wb_err);
 	if (verf)
 		nfsd_copy_write_verifier(verf, nn);
